  {
    "date": "2024-07-10",
    "term": "会う",
    "kana": "あう",
    "meaning": "to meet, to see",
    "level": "N5",
    "pos": ["Godan verb with 'u' ending", "intransitive verb"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news2", "nf26"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["sound-change", "unclear"],
    "headline": "Au has no settled origin: one theory has it imitating the sound of the upper and lower lips meeting.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Inherited from Old Japanese, from Proto-Japonic *ap-. Further etymology uncertain. Theories of earliest origin include:"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Imitative of the upper and lower lips meeting"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Shortened from 二肖経 (フタアエフ futa aefu, two go-together)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Shortened from アアフツ (aa futsu), the latter portion a variant of 二(ふた)つ (futatsu, “two”)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Either 間(あい) (ai, “relation”) → 逢(あふ) (afu, “meeting”) → 会(あう) (au) or 逢(あふ) (afu) → 間(あい) (ai) → 会(あう) (au)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Various forms of あう (合, 会, 逢, 遭; “join; be together; meet”) are attested from the Middle Ages (c. 1185-1573). Compare 合(あ)う (au)."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
