    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese 過ぐ (sugu). First attested in the Kojiki of 712."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Likely cognate with 挿(す)げる (sugeru, “to pass a hole through something”), 直(す)ぐ (sugu, “straight; soon”, adverb)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Reconstructed as deriving from Proto-Japonic *sunk-oi-."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Development"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Natural progression from Old and Classical Japanese 上(かみ)二(に)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (kami nidan katsuyō, “upper bigrade conjugation”) verbs ending in -u to modern Japanese 上(かみ)一(いち)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (kami ichidan katsuyō, “upper monograde conjugation”) verbs ending in -iru."
      }
    ],
