  {
    "date": "2024-07-22",
    "term": "朝",
    "kana": "あさ",
    "meaning": "morning",
    "level": "N5",
    "pos": ["noun (common) (futsuumeishi)", "adverb (fukushi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news1", "nf09"],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["borrowing", "sound-change"],
    "headline": "Asa is attested in the Man'yōshū of 759, and its old day cycle began in the afternoon.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese, from Proto-Japonic *asa. Attested in the Man'yōshū of 759."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Historically, a day was split into two halves:"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Afternoon cycle: 朝(あさ) (asa) → 昼(ひる) (hiru) → 夕(ゆう) (yū)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "* Evening cycle: 夕(ゆう)べ (yūbe) → 宵(よい) (yoi) → 夜(よ)中(なか) (yonaka) → 暁(あかつき) (akatsuki) → 朝(あした) (ashita)"
      },
      {
        "quote": "While asa and ashita represent the same time period, asa was associated with beginning of the afternoon and ashita was associated with the end of the night. Both terms share an initial as- and are likely etymologically related."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Beyond Japonic, possibly related to Middle Korean 아ᄎᆞᆷ〮 (àchóm, “morning”) > Korean 아침 (achim). Alexander Vovin believes this is a Koreanic borrowing into Japanese, identifying Japanese つとめて (tsutomete) as the native Japonic root for \"morning\" (Vovin 2010, p. 224)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "* However, つとめて (tsutomete) is not attested until the late 800s or early 900s, although root 夙(つと) (tsuto) as in 夙(つと)に (tsuto ni, “early in the morning”, adverb) appears in the Man'yōshū of 759."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Alternatively, may be cognate with adjective 浅(あさ)い (asai, “shallow; early”), verbs 浅(あ)せる (aseru, “to become shallow”) and 褪(あ)せる (aseru, “to fade, to become pale”)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "* The concepts of \"shallow\" and \"deep\" are used in other respects relative to time, such as 夜更(よふ)かし (yofukashi, “staying up late into the night”) and 夜(よ)更(ふ)け (yofuke, “very late at night”), where the fuk- root in both terms is from 深(ふか)い (fukai, “deep; late, long-lasting”)."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "id": 126241,
        "ja": "朝に弱いんです。",
        "en": "I am not a morning person.",
        "enId": 277752,
        "form": "朝",
        "furigana": [["朝", "あさ"], ["に"], ["弱", "よわ"], ["いんです。"]]
      },
      {
        "id": 126225,
        "ja": "朝は空気が新鮮だ。",
